course: dictionary
lesson: 15027
title: Restful: calm and relaxing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Restful describes something that helps you relax, feel calm, and rest. Look at the words near it for clues. «We had a restful night after the long drive.» After a long drive, you would want to relax and sleep well, so restful must mean calm and good for resting.
explain: Restful can describe places, colours, music, or a whole holiday. «The hotel room had restful colours, soft green and pale blue.» The colours are soft and gentle, so they help you feel calm. Always ask: would a calm feeling fit here? If yes, you have found the meaning.
explain: Restful is not the same as tired. Tired means you need rest. Restful means something gives you rest or helps you relax. A sleepy person is tired, but a restful place is one that makes you feel calm.
fact: Restful means calm and peaceful, helping you to relax.
fact: Restful can also mean giving good rest, such as restful sleep.
fact: «A restful night» means a night of good, calm sleep.
fact: Restful is an adjective, and it can change form: restful, more restful, most restful.
fact: Words like peaceful and calm are close in meaning to restful, but restful is about how something helps you rest.
exercise: «The hotel room had restful colours, soft green and pale blue.» What does restful mean here? | *Calm and peaceful | Bright and loud | Very fast | Dirty and dark
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the night: «We had a restful night after the long drive.» | long | after | drive | *restful
exercise: Mia says restful is just another word for sleepy. Why might an author choose restful? | *It means calm and helps you relax, which is different from just tired | It means exactly the same as tired | It is a longer word | It means noisy and busy
test: «The restful holiday gave the family time to relax.» What does restful suggest? | Cold and wet | *Calm and relaxing | Busy and rushed | Noisy and loud
test: Which word could replace restful in «a restful night»? | noisy | *peaceful | rushed | cold
exam: «After a restful sleep, Sam felt ready for school.» What does restful mean here? | *Giving good rest | Very hungry | Full of noise | Wet and grey
